1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,987
Hi, this is Gemihub Hybrid: local answers, connected communities.

2
00:00:04,987 --> 00:00:17,325
Our existing platform, gemihub, already lets independent neighborhood shops create their own bespoke websites and booking pages simply by chatting with AI, with no templates and no web agency needed.

3
00:00:17,325 --> 00:00:19,950
A town guide then connects those shops together.

4
00:00:19,950 --> 00:00:30,862
Here is the problem: once a shop publishes its site, sending every routine question like opening hours to a cloud LLM creates unpredictable traffic costs for a small business.

5
00:00:30,862 --> 00:00:43,087
For Build Hybrid AI 2026, I extended gemihub with a Firebase AI Logic hybrid inference layer for both the town guide and shop assistants, with no visitor API keys required.

6
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:52,500
On supported Chrome devices, the app probes Gemini Nano availability at startup so the very first turn runs locally with prefer on-device mode.

7
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:05,500
Gemini Nano streams answers about a shop's published facts right in the browser, and every reply displays an inline telemetry pill from the Firebase AI Logic SDK: On-device, model, latency, and routing reason, with zero cloud cost for common FAQs.

8
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Comparisons across shops, allergy or price questions, and follow-ups route to cloud-only mode with Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite, protected by Firebase App Check and tunable via Remote Config.

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:27,500
The town guide also exposes a public read-only MCP endpoint at /api/mcp, so external agents can discover published shops and local events.

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Inside Robata Akari's own assistant, booking starts on-device too.

11
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:46,500
When a visitor says they want to book for Friday without a time or party size, Gemini Nano extracts the partial slots as structured JSON, and deterministic code asks for the missing details, still with zero cloud calls.

12
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:55,000
Once the date, time, and party size are complete, the chat hands off to the cloud.

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Existing deterministic MCP tools check live seats and pricing, and the confirmation modal ensures the model never confirms a reservation on its own.

14
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:19,500
And if a visitor's browser doesn't support Gemini Nano, or while the model is still downloading, chat never blocks.

15
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:25,000
Firebase AI Logic falls back cleanly to the cloud and labels it honestly.

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:34,500
Try the live demo at hybrid.gemihub.net, and check out our Apache-2.0 licensed code on GitHub.

17
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,000
Thanks for watching!
